# LLM Assessment Deduplication Safety

## Rule

Before any LLM API call, the orchestrator MUST check the LLM database for
existing usable results for that `(site_id, prompt_key)` pair.

## What counts as "usable"

| Tier | Table | Usable if |
|------|-------|-----------|
| Exclusionary (E1-E9) | `screening_verdicts` | `verdict` in (`pass`, `fail`) |
| Avoidance (A1-A15) | `screening_verdicts` | `verdict` in (`pass`, `fail`, `caution`) |
| Ranking (NH-*, HI-*, etc.) | `ranking_scores` | `score IS NOT NULL` |

An `inconclusive` verdict is NOT usable — the system will re-attempt.

## Behaviour

- If usable data exists → skip the API call, log a structured `llm_assess_skipped` event.
- If no usable data exists → proceed with the API call.
- This applies to ALL tiers and ALL run modes (standard `run()`, `run_sequential_elimination()`, `run_second_pass()`).

## Force re-run

- The `--force-rerun` CLI flag bypasses dedup checks.
- When `--force-rerun` is used, display existing data summary and require interactive `click.confirm()` before proceeding.
- NEVER silently overwrite existing data without explicit user consent.

## Logging

All skipped assessments must be logged to `logs/llm/<run_id>/skips/` as structured JSON with:
`run_id`, `site_id`, `site_name`, `criterion_id`, `prompt_key`, `skip_reason`, `existing_verdict`, `existing_confidence`, `existing_run_id`.
